From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Narfinger <Narfinger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 12:58:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] backport: deny: Allow chrono in cargo deny (#50002)

Chrono is unmaintained. We need to switch to time or jiff.
This fixes the merge queue.

Testing: No tests for deny.

Signed-off-by: Narfinger <Narfinger@users.noreply.github.com>

Fork note: upstream 60d9b3ecb68, which came after Servo 0.8.0, backported
unchanged. On 0.8.0 the cargo-deny step of `./mach test-tidy` fails on
this advisory too. Upstream replaced chrono with jiff afterwards (#50004),
which this fork doesn't carry. Drop this patch at the first sync onto a
release that contains #50002, where it applies empty, or is superseded
by #50004.

Validation: `./mach test-tidy` on ohos-main 8ca6843c7f9 with this commit and the previous two: no errors (before them, the cargo-deny step reported the libsqlite3-sys, libz-sys and chrono advisories).
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; backported unchanged by the agent)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 deny.toml | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/deny.toml b/deny.toml
index 7e295b5fa46..1269bcdce3d 100644
--- a/deny.toml
+++ b/deny.toml
@@ -53,6 +53,8 @@ ignore = [
     # rusqlite can not be independently updated as sea-query-rusqlite needs update.
     "RUSTSEC-2026-0459",
 
+    # chrono is unmaintained and will be replaced by probably jiff.
+    "RUSTSEC-2026-0543",
 ]
 
 # This section is considered when running `cargo deny check licenses`
